# {{ title }}

Each file in this folder shows one area of YAMD. Open any of them and run **YAMD: Open Preview to the Side** (:kbd[Cmd+K V]) to see the rendered result.

Start with the [guided tour](getting-started.yamd), then explore by topic.

::toc{depth=2}

## Status key

| Status    | Meaning                                                                 |
| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Available | Works in the current extension                                          |

## Basics

| Example                                                     | Shows                                                               | Status    |
| ----------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------- |
| [Text and paragraphs](01-basics/text-and-paragraphs.yamd)   | Line breaks, emphasis family, spans, escaping                       | Available |
| [Headings and lists](01-basics/headings-and-lists.yamd)     | Heading IDs, bullets, numbering, nesting, tasks                     | Available |
| [Links and images](01-basics/links-and-images.yamd)         | Inline, reference, bare and wiki links; images, figures             | Available |
| [Tables](01-basics/tables.yamd)                             | Pipe tables, alignment, captions, colspan, list tables              | Available |
| [Code and math](01-basics/code-and-math.yamd)               | Fences with attributes, diagrams, inline and block math             | Available |
| [Reference links](01-basics/ref-links.yamd)                  | `ref=` spans pointing at labeled text elsewhere in the note, a flow chart | Available |

